From 89d62b8ee05f98d0665297bc3d7466dfc763c247 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 04:33:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] 16-bit image blocks: context rANS over the residual
 words, block codec 34, opt-in (KOLMO_NATIVE=rans)

A block with the 16-bit image transform (flag 6) is a header, the low-byte plane and the high-byte
plane of the zigzag residuals; the block codec (zstd, BWT) codes the planes without the image's
geometry. Codec 34 stores the header, skip and trailing bytes and codes the residuals as
(high, low) byte pairs with the codec 33 coder under the half-octave classes of the four
neighbouring words (mk 3), the low byte also under its high byte. The block worker tries it beside
the block codec when the opt-in is set and keeps the smaller; the decoder rebuilds the transformed
stream and the image inverse is unchanged. Version 11 frames; valid only with transform flag 6,
refused inside a graph. No default output changes.

krans: the words hint of the encoder (order 0 per byte of the word, then the word contexts; eq 3
at effort 2) and a decoder run for whole words that carries three of the four neighbour classes
from the word before.

Tests: tests/test_krans.c (words hint, odd lengths, odd segments, other lags), tests/test_krans_frames.c
(codecs 33 and 34 inside the container: leaves, block payloads, whole frames in every mode, 1 and 4
threads, range reads, version-10 header, damaged payloads and frames; plain and ASan/UBSan),
tests/test_krans_modes.py (a headerless 16-bit image). memneed row for codec 34.

Review R02, claim img16-ctx-rans (#17).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FUEN4aRWhUw7yL7cZMqTmZ
